    guard: "her missing husband", ev: ["the camp fire", "a rumour about deportation", "the youngest fell ill"], mood: ["very soft", "numb", "tearful"],
    mse: "Thin, worn clothes, headscarf | Still, startles at shouts outside | Very soft, through interpreter | 'Fire inside' | Low, constricted | Coherent | Hopelessness, ambiguous loss, fear for children | Flashbacks, no psychosis | Oriented | Partial insight",
    dx: "Post-traumatic stress disorder with a depressive episode in a refugee, with ambiguous loss",
    ddx: [["Somatic symptom disorder", "Body pain is a common idiom of distress; the full pattern of intrusions, avoidance and low mood points to PTSD and depression"], ["Anaemia causing tiredness and pain", "Anaemia needs treatment, but it does not explain flashbacks and hopelessness"], ["Normal reaction to hardship", "Six years of persistent, disabling symptoms need treatment alongside practical help"]],
    rubric: ["Used a trained interpreter and checked her preference for a female clinician", "Built safety and rapport, putting practical needs first", "Explored trauma symptoms and losses gently", "Asked about suicide and the children's safety clearly", "Planned culturally adapted care with NGO, food, shelter and school links"],
    traps: ["somatic_mask", "cultural_idiom"], protect: ["children", "NGO health worker", "camp community"],
